Column name: sid Type: STRING Description: Storm Identifier.
Column name: season Type: STRING
Column name: number Type: INT64 Description: The cardinal number of the system for that season. The count includes all basins/nso this will not be continuous for basin files.
Column name: basin Type: STRING Description: Basins include: NA - North Atlantic EP - Eastern North Pacific WP - Western North Pacific NI - North Indian SI - South Indian SP - Southern Pacific SA - South Atlantic MM - Missing - should not appear in final IBTrACS product
Column name: subbasin Type: STRING Description: Subbasins include: MM - missing - no sub basin for this basin (no subbasins provided for WP/nSI) CS - Caribbean Sea GM - Gulf of Mexico CP - Central Pacific BB - Bay of Bengal AS - Arabian Sea WA - Western Australia EA - Eastern Australia
Column name: name Type: STRING Description: Name provided by the agency. IBTrACS ignores most names that include digits or abbreviations.
Column name: iso_time Type: TIMESTAMP Description: ISO Time provided in Universal Time Coordinates (UTC). Format is YYYY-MM-DD HH:mm:ss Most points are provided at 6 hour intervals. Some agencies provided 3 hour points (e.g./nNew Delhi) or times at important observations (e.g./nlandfall times in the North Atlantic/netc.).
Column name: nature Type: STRING Description: Combined storm type. This is assigned based on all available storm types. They include: DS - Disturbance TS - Tropical ET - Extratropical SS - Subtropical NR - Not reported MX - Mixture (contradicting nature reports from different agencies)
Column name: latitude Type: FLOAT64
Column name: longitude Type: FLOAT64
Column name: wmo_wind Type: INT64 Description: Maximum sustained wind speed from the WMO agency for the current location. NO adjustment is made for differences in wind speed averaging periods. hurdat/atcf = North Atlantic - U.S. Miami (NOAA NHC) - 1-minute winds tokyo = RSMC Tokyo (JMA) - 10-minute newdelhi = RSMC New Delhi (IMD) - 3-minute reunion = RSMC La Reunion (MFLR) - 10 minute bom = Australian TCWCs (TCWC Perth/nDarwin/nBrisbane) - 10-minute nadi = RSMC Nadi (FMS) - 10 minute wellington = TCWC Wellington (NZMS) - 10-minute
Column name: wmo_pressure Type: INT64
Column name: wmo_agency Type: STRING Description: This is the reporting agency responsible for the basin as currently listed. It should be noted that many of the agencies did not accept official WMO responsibility until relatively recently/ne.g./nLa Reunion in 1993 or IMD in 1990. Therefore the WMO agency is used loosely todescribe the currently reponsible agency.
Column name: track_type Type: STRING Description: Track type Tropical storms can interact. This identifies : PROVISIONAL - Real time data used to populate the position and other parameters of this system. This is a provisional track that will be replaced when reanalysis of the storm is performed. (Usually within 2 years of the storm's occurence) main - primary track associated with a storm system. spur - usually short lived tracks associated with a main track and either represent alternate positions at the beginning of a system. Can also represent actual system interactions (e.g./nFujiwhara interactions).
Column name: dist2land Type: INT64 Description: Distance to land from the current position. The land dataset includes all continents and any islands larger than XX. The distance is the nearest at the present time in any direction.
Column name: landfall Type: INT64 Description: Nearest location to land within next 6 hours. This can be thought of a landfall flag: =0 -- Landfall within 6 hours. >0 -- No landfall within next 6 hours. Calculations are based on storm center (columns 9,10). Values less than 60 nmile likely are impacted by the system even though the center of the system is not over land. The uses the same land mask as DIST2LAND.
Column name: iflag Type: STRING Description: Interpolation Flag A 14 character flag string which denotes the source of each agency's report: Interpolation Flags include: _ == missing reports. No information provided. O == original report as provided by the agency. P == position was interpolated (all variables were interpolated/filled/nincluding intensity) I == Position was provided/nbut Intensity variables (and likely other variables) were interpolated/filled V = Position and intensity variables are original but some variables were interpolated/filled. The order of the 14 characters refers to the following 14 datasets: 1 - USA Agency (see column 18) 2 - Tokyo 3 - CMA 4 - HKO 5 - NewDelhi 6 - Reunion 7 - BoM 8 - Nadi 9 - Wellington 10 - ds824 11 - TD9636 12 - TD9635 13 - Neumann Southern Hemisphere data set 14 - M.L. Chenoweth N Atlantic Historic dataset
Column name: usa_agency Type: STRING Description: The agency file providing the information: The representative US agency data is derived from a hierarchical selection: the first dataset in the following list to provide information at the given time is used as the USA_agency: - HURDAT_ATL - HURSAT_EPA - ATCF (for NA and EP basins only) - JTWC_WP - JTWC_IO - JTWC_EP - JTWC_CP - JTWC_SH - CPHC [separate file provided by CPHC for years TBD] - tcvitals - THIS INDICATES THAT THE DATA ARE PRELIMINARY While these agencies are generally orthogonal/nthere are cases where a system is provided in more than one source. In this case/nthe report from the highest source is used. ATCF format info from: https://www.nrlmry.navy.mil/atcf_web/docs/database/new/abdeck.txt HURDAT2 info from: http://www.nhc.noaa.gov/data/hurdat/hurdat2-format-atlantic.pdf
Column name: usa_latitude Type: FLOAT64
Column name: usa_longitude Type: FLOAT64
Column name: usa_record Type: STRING Description: Record identifier (see notes below) C – Closest approach to a coast/nnot followed by a landfall G – Genesis I – An intensity peak in terms of both pressure and wind L – Landfall (center of system crossing a coastline) P – Minimum in central pressure R – Provides additional detail on the intensity of the cyclone when rapid changes are underway S – Change of status of the system T – Provides additional detail on the track (position) of the cyclone W – Maximum sustained wind speed
Column name: usa_status Type: STRING Description: Status of system. Options are:  DB - disturbance/n TD - tropical depression/n TS - tropical storm/n TY - typhoon/n ST - super typhoon/n TC - tropical cyclone/n HU,HR - hurricane/n SD - subtropical depression/n SS - subtropical storm/n EX - extratropical systems/n PT - post tropical/n IN - inland/n DS - dissipating/n LO - low/n WV - tropical wave/n ET - extrapolated/n MD - monsoon depression/n XX - unknown.
Column name: usa_wind Type: INT64 Description: Maximum sustained wind speed in knots: 0 - 300 kts.
Column name: usa_pressure Type: INT64 Description: Minimum central pressure (mb)
Column name: usa_sshs Type: INT64 Description: Saffir-Simpson Hurricane Scale information based on the wind speed provided by the US agency wind speed (US agencies provide 1-minute wind speeds) -5 = Unknown [XX] -4 = Post-tropical [EX/nET/nPT] -3 = Miscellaneous disturbances [WV/nLO/nDB/nDS/nIN/nMD] -2 = Subtropical [SS/nSD] Tropical systems classified based on wind speeds [TD/nTS/nHU/nTY,/nTC/nST/nHR]  -1 = Tropical depression (W<34)  0 = Tropical storm [34<W<64]  1 = Category 1 [64<=W<83]  2 = Category 2 [83<=W<96]  3 = Category 3 [96<=W<113]  4 = Category 4 [113<=W<137]  5 = Category 5 [W >= 137]
Column name: usa_r34_ne Type: INT64 Description: – 34 kt wind radii maximum extent in northeastern quadrant
Column name: usa_r34_se Type: INT64 Description: 34 kt wind radii maximum extent in southeastern quadrant
Column name: usa_r34_sw Type: INT64 Description: – 34 kt wind radii maximum extent in southwestern quadrant
Column name: usa_r34_nw Type: INT64 Description: – 34 kt wind radii maximum extent in northwestern quadrant
Column name: usa_r50_ne Type: INT64 Description: 50 kt wind radii maximum extent in northeastern quadrant
Column name: usa_r50_se Type: INT64 Description: – 50 kt wind radii maximum extent in southeastern quadrant
Column name: usa_r50_sw Type: INT64 Description: – 50 kt wind radii maximum extent in southwestern quadrant
Column name: usa_r50_nw Type: INT64 Description: 50 kt wind radii maximum extent in northwestern quadrant
Column name: usa_r64_ne Type: INT64 Description: – 64 kt wind radii maximum extent in northeastern quadrant
Column name: usa_r64_se Type: INT64 Description: 64 kt wind radii maximum extent in southeastern quadrant
Column name: usa_r64_sw Type: INT64 Description: – 64 kt wind radii maximum extent in southwestern quadrant
Column name: usa_r64_nw Type: INT64 Description: 64 kt wind radii maximum extent in northwestern quadrant
Column name: usa_poci Type: INT64 Description: pressure in millibars of the last closed isobar/n900 - 1050 mb NOT BEST-TRACKED (not reanalyzed)
Column name: usa_roci Type: INT64 Description: radius of the last closed isobar/n0 - 999 n mi. NOT BEST TRACKED (not reanalyzed)
Column name: usa_rmw Type: INT64 Description: radius of max winds/n0 - 999 n mi. NOT BEST TRACKED (not reanalyzed)
Column name: usa_eye Type: STRING Description: eye diameter/n0 - 120 n mi. NOT BEST TRACKED (not reanalyzed)
Column name: tokyo_latitude Type: FLOAT64
Column name: tokyo_longitude Type: FLOAT64
Column name: tokyo_grade Type: INT64 Description: <Grade> 1 : Not used  2 : Tropical Depression (TD)  3 : Tropical Storm (TS)  4 : Severe Tropical Storm (STS)  5 : Typhoon (TY)  6 : Extratropical Cyclone (L)  7 : Just entering into the responsible area of  Japan Meteorological Agency (JMA)  8 : Not used  9 : Tropical Cyclone of TS intensity or higher
Column name: tokyo_wind Type: INT64 Description: Maximum sustained wind speed [10-min averaging period]
Column name: tokyo_pressure Type: INT64 Description: Central pressure
Column name: tokyo_r50_dir Type: INT64 Description: 1 : Northeast (NE)  2 : East (E)  3 : Southeast (SE)  4 : South (S)  5 : Southwest (SW)  6 : West (W)  7 : Northwest (NW)  8 : North (N)  9 : (symmetric circle)
Column name: tokyo_r50_longitude Type: INT64 Description: The longest radius of 50kt winds or greater
Column name: tokyo_r50_short Type: INT64 Description: The shortest radius of 50kt winds or greater
Column name: tokyo_r30_dir Type: INT64 Description: 1 : Northeast (NE)  2 : East (E)  3 : Southeast (SE)  4 : South (S)  5 : Southwest (SW)  6 : West (W)  7 : Northwest (NW)  8 : North (N)  9 : (symmetric circle)
Column name: tokyo_r30_long Type: INT64 Description: The longest radius of 30kt winds or greater
Column name: tokyo_r30_short Type: INT64 Description: The shortest radius of 30kt winds or greater
Column name: tokyo_land Type: INT64 Description: <Indicator of landfall or passage>  Landfall or passage over the Japanese islands occurred within  one hour after the time of the analysis with this indicator.
Column name: cma_latitude Type: FLOAT64 Description: Latitude from Chinese Meteorological Administration data from Shanghai Typhoon Institute
Column name: cma_longitude Type: FLOAT64 Description: Longitude from Chinese Meteorological Administration data from Shanghai Typhoon Institute
Column name: cma_cat Type: INT64 Description: Intensity category according to the Chinese National Standard for Grade of Tropical Cyclones (which has been used since 15 June 2006): 0 –– Weaker than Tropical Depression or unknown intensity; 1 –– Tropical Depression (TD: 10.8–17.1 m/s); 2 –– Tropical Storm (TS:17.2–24.4 m/s); 3 –– Severe Tropical Storm (STS: 24.5–32.6 m/s); 4 –– Typhoon (TY: 32.7–41.4 m/s); 5 –– Severe Typhoon (STY: 41.5–50.9 m/s); 6 –– Super Typhoon (SuperTY: ≥51.0 m/s); 9 –– Extratropical Cyclone (ET) stage.
Column name: cma_wind Type: INT64 Description: Two-minute mean maximum sustained wind (MSW; m/s) near the TC center. WND = 9 indicates MSW < 10 m/s/nWND = 0 indicates unknown intensity
Column name: cma_pressure Type: INT64 Description: Minimum pressure (hPa) near the TC center.
Column name: hko_latitude Type: STRING Description: Latitude from Hong Kong Observatory
Column name: hko_longitude Type: FLOAT64 Description: Longitude from Hong Kong Observatory
Column name: hko_cat Type: STRING Description: After 2009/nwe further classified two more storm types above typhoon/nso there are in total 7 storm types LW (Low) <22 kt TD (Tropical Depression) 22 – 33 kt TS (Tropical Storm) 34 – 47 kt STS (Severe Tropical Storm) 48 – 63 kt T (Typhoon) 64 – 80 kt ST (Severe Typhoon) 81 – 99 kt SuperT (Super Typhoon) >= 100 kt
Column name: hko_wind Type: INT64
Column name: hko_pressure Type: INT64
Column name: newdelhi_latitude Type: FLOAT64
Column name: newdelhi_longitude Type: FLOAT64
Column name: newdelhi_grade Type: STRING Description: Types of disturbances: Low pressure area W<17 knots D - Depression 17<=W<28 DD - Deep Depression 28<=W<34 CS - Cyclonic Storm 34<=W<48 SCS - Severe Cyclonic Storm 48<=W<64 VSCS - Very Severe Cyclonic Storm 64<=W<120 SCS - Super Cyclonic Storm W>=120 knots
Column name: newdelhi_wind Type: INT64
Column name: newdelhi_pressure Type: INT64
Column name: newdelhi_ci Type: FLOAT64
Column name: newdelhi_dp Type: INT64
Column name: newdelhi_poci Type: INT64
Column name: reunion_latitude Type: FLOAT64
Column name: reunion_longitude Type: FLOAT64
Column name: reunion_type Type: INT64 Description: 01= tropics; disturbance ( no closed isobars)  02= <34 knot winds/n<17m/s winds and at least one closed isobar  03= 34-63 knots/n17-32m/s  04= >63 knots/n>32m/s  05= extratropical  06= dissipating  07= subtropical cyclone (nonfrontal/nlow pressure system that comprises  initially baroclinic circulation developing over subtropical water)  08= overland  09= unknown
Column name: reunion_wind Type: INT64 Description: Maximum average wind speed
Column name: reunion_pressure Type: INT64 Description: Central pressure
Column name: reunion_tnum Type: FLOAT64 Description: Dvorak T-number
Column name: reunion_ci Type: FLOAT64 Description: Dvorak CI-number
Column name: reunion_rmw Type: INT64 Description: Radius of maximum winds
Column name: reunion_r34_ne Type: INT64 Description: 34 kt wind radii maximum extent in northeastern quadrant
Column name: reunion_r34_se Type: INT64 Description: 34 kt wind radii maximum extent in southeastern quadrant
Column name: reunion_r34_sw Type: INT64 Description: 34 kt wind radii maximum extent in southwestern quadrant
Column name: reunion_r34_nw Type: INT64 Description: 34 kt wind radii maximum extent in northwestern quadrant
Column name: reunion_r50_ne Type: INT64 Description: 50 kt wind radii maximum extent in northeastern quadrant
Column name: reunion_r50_se Type: INT64 Description: 50 kt wind radii maximum extent in southeastern quadrant
Column name: reunion_r50_sw Type: INT64 Description: 50 kt wind radii maximum extent in southwestern quadrant
Column name: reunion_r50_nw Type: INT64 Description: 50 kt wind radii maximum extent in northwestern quadrant
Column name: reunion_r64_ne Type: INT64 Description: 64 kt wind radii maximum extent in northeastern quadrant
Column name: reunion_r64_se Type: INT64 Description: 64 kt wind radii maximum extent in southeastern quadrant
Column name: reunion_r64_sw Type: INT64 Description: 64 kt wind radii maximum extent in southwestern quadrant
Column name: reunion_r64_nw Type: INT64 Description: 64 kt wind radii maximum extent in northwestern quadrant
Column name: bom_latitude Type: FLOAT64 Description: Latitude from Australian Bureau of Meterology
Column name: bom_longitude Type: FLOAT64 Description: Longitude from Australian Bureau of Meterology
Column name: bom_type Type: INT64 Description: This indicates the type of system that this cyclone was at the time of the observation. Note that cyclones can evolve during their lifetimes and hence change type mid-stream (e.g. Extratropical transition (ETT))
Column name: bom_wind Type: INT64 Description: This is the estimated maximum mean wind around the cyclone – that is in the vicinity of the centre.
Column name: bom_pressure Type: INT64 Description: Central pressure of the cyclone
Column name: bom_tnum Type: FLOAT64
Column name: bom_ci Type: FLOAT64
Column name: bom_rmw Type: INT64 Description: This is the mean radius (from the system centre) of the maximum mean wind.
Column name: bom_r34_ne Type: INT64 Description: This is the mean radius (from the system centre) of the extent of winds; gale-force (17m/s) or above. The four sectors show the mean extent in the respective quadrant centred on the cardinal point. Northeast quadrant
Column name: bom_r34_se Type: INT64 Description: This is the mean radius (from the system centre) of the extent of winds; gale-force (17m/s) or above. The four sectors show the mean extent in the respective quadrant centred on the cardinal point. Southeast quadrant
Column name: bom_r34_sw Type: INT64 Description: This is the mean radius (from the system centre) of the extent of winds; gale-force (17m/s) or above. The four sectors show the mean extent in the respective quadrant centred on the cardinal point. Southwest quadrant
Column name: bom_r34_nw Type: INT64 Description: This is the mean radius (from the system centre) of the extent of winds; gale-force (17m/s) or above. The four sectors show the mean extent in the respective quadrant centred on the cardinal point. Northwest quadrant
Column name: bom_r50_ne Type: INT64 Description: These are the mean radius (from the system centre) of the extent of winds; storm-force (25m/s) or above. Northeast quadrant.
Column name: bom_r50_se Type: INT64 Description: These are the mean radius (from the system centre) of the extent of winds; storm-force (25m/s) or above. Southeast quadrant.
Column name: bom_r50_sw Type: INT64 Description: These are the mean radius (from the system centre) of the extent of winds; storm-force (25m/s) or above. Southwest quadrant.
Column name: bom_r50_nw Type: INT64 Description: These are the mean radius (from the system centre) of the extent of winds; storm-force (25m/s) or above. Northwest quadrant.
Column name: bom_r64_ne Type: INT64 Description: These are the mean radius (from the system centre) of the extent of winds; hurricane-force (33m/s) or above. Northeast quadrant
Column name: bom_r64_se Type: INT64 Description: These are the mean radius (from the system centre) of the extent of winds; hurricane-force (33m/s) or above. Southeast quadrant
Column name: bom_r64_sw Type: INT64 Description: These are the mean radius (from the system centre) of the extent of winds; hurricane-force (33m/s) or above. Southwest quadrant
Column name: bom_r64_nw Type: INT64 Description: These are the mean radius (from the system centre) of the extent of winds; hurricane-force (33m/s) or above. Northwest quadrant
Column name: bom_roci Type: INT64 Description: The estimated mean radius of the outermost closed isobar (1-hPa spacing).
Column name: bom_poci Type: INT64 Description: Environmental pressure in which the cyclone is embedded
Column name: bom_eye Type: INT64 Description: Mean radius of the cyclone eye.
Column name: bom_pos_method Type: INT64 Description: This indicates the tools that were used to derive the centre location of the system. ADAM Code Method to derive position NULL Default - unknown 1 no sat/nno rad/nno obs 2 no sat/nno rad/nobs only 3 Sat IR/Vis; no clear eye 4 Sat IR/Vis; clearly defined eye 5 aircraft radar report 6 land-based radar report 7 Sat IR/Vis & rad & obs 8 report inside eye 10 Sat- Scatterometer 11 Sat- Microwave 12 Manned Aircraft Reconnaissance 13 UAV Aircraft Reconnaissance
Column name: bom_pressure_method Type: INT64 Description: This code may need to be expanded to handle new systems in the future/nand also to differentiate between pressure-wind relationships used to derive the central pressure. ADAM code Method WMO Code NULL Unknown or N/A 1 Aircraft or Dropsonde  observation 1 2 Over water observation (e.g.  buoy) 2 3 Over land observation 3 4 Instrument – unknown type 5 5 Derived Directly from DVORAK 4 6 Derived from wind via a P-W  equation 5 7 Estimate from surrounding obs 5 8 Extrapolation from radar 5 9 Other 5
Column name: wellington_latitude Type: FLOAT64
Column name: wellington_longitude Type: FLOAT64
Column name: wellington_wind Type: INT64
Column name: wellington_pressure Type: INT64
Column name: nadi_latitude Type: FLOAT64 Description: Latitude from Fiji Meteorological Service data from RSMC Hadi
Column name: nadi_longitude Type: FLOAT64 Description: Longitude from Fiji Meteorological Service data from RSMC Hadi
Column name: nadi_cat Type: INT64 Description: Nadi assigned category
Column name: nadi_wind Type: INT64
Column name: nadi_pressure Type: INT64
Column name: ds824_latitude Type: FLOAT64 Description: Latitude from DataSet 824 - A historic dataset with data from the 1800s through 1980(ish)
Column name: ds824_longitude Type: FLOAT64 Description: Longitude from DataSet 824 - A historic dataset with data from the 1800s through 1980(ish)
Column name: ds824_stage Type: STRING Description: TC - Tropical cyclone
Column name: ds824_wind Type: INT64
Column name: ds824_pressure Type: INT64
Column name: td9636_latitude Type: FLOAT64 Description: Latitude from Dataset of a collection of global storms (1842-1980)
Column name: td9636_longitude Type: FLOAT64 Description: Longitude from Dataset of a collection of global storms (1842-1980)
Column name: td9636_stage Type: INT64 Description: This field gives an estimate of the highest winds occurring in the storm at the time and location indicated. The entire storm was coded as to the highest stage reached for some of the earlier years. 0 - Tropical disturbance (1969 onward) 1 - depression < 34 [some variation in definition for S Indian] 2 - Storm 34-63 [with some variation in definition for S Indian] 3 - point where wind reached 64 knots [except N Indian where it is wind 43-47 knots] 4 - Hurricane > 64 [except in N Indian/nWind > 48] 5 - Extratropical 6 - Dissipating 7 - Unknown Intensity or doubtful track
Column name: td9636_wind Type: INT64 Description: Estimated highest wind speed at the time indicated. These estimates are subjective and must be interpreted with caution.
Column name: td9636_pressure Type: INT64
Column name: td9635_latitude Type: FLOAT64 Description: Latitude from Dataset of a collection of western Pacific Storms (~1945-1976)
Column name: td9635_longitude Type: FLOAT64 Description: Longitude from Dataset of a collection of western Pacific Storms (~1945-1976)
Column name: td9635_wind Type: FLOAT64
Column name: td9635_pressure Type: INT64
Column name: td9635_roci Type: INT64 Description: Size. (Radius of system)
Column name: neumann_latitude Type: FLOAT64
Column name: neumann_longitude Type: FLOAT64
Column name: neumann_class Type: STRING Description: EX - Extratropical TC - Tropical MM - Missing
Column name: neumann_wind Type: INT64
Column name: neumann_pressure Type: INT64
Column name: mlc_latitude Type: FLOAT64 Description: Latitude from Mike Chenoweth data with updated data for the North Atlantic for the 1800s.
Column name: mlc_longitude Type: FLOAT64 Description: Longitude from Mike Chenoweth data with updated data for the North Atlantic for the 1800s.
Column name: mlc_class Type: STRING Description: Storm classification EX - Extratropical HU - Hurricane LO - Low MH SD - Subtropical depression SS - Subtropical storm TD - Tropical Depression TS - Tropical Storm TW WV - Open Wave
Column name: mlc_wind Type: INT64
Column name: mlc_pressure Type: INT64
Column name: usa_atcf_id Type: STRING Description: The ATCF ID is assigned by US agencies and can be used to comparethe storm with other US cyclone-related datasets. If two (or more) ATCF tracks make up one storm/nthen the IDs are separated by a colon. The format of the ATCF ID is B<bb><nn><yyyy> where bb is the basin ID/nnn is the number of the storm in that basin and yyyy is the year. Possible basin values are: AL: North Atlantic/nSL: South Atlantic/nEP: East Pacific/nWP: West Pacific/nSH: Southern Hemisphere/nIO: North Indian For the provisional data/nother basin identifiers were provided that include: CP: Central Pacific/nSP: South Pacific/nSI: South Indian/nAS: Arabian Sea (North Indian) and BB: Bay of Bengal (North Indian)
Column name: source_url Type: STRING Description: Source 
Column name: etl_timestamp Type: TIMESTAMP Description: Load time for this data row
